<title>GERMANY: Prodi sees devaluation if Italy outside EMU in '99.</title>
<headline>Prodi sees devaluation if Italy outside EMU in '99.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian prime minister Romano Prodi warned of serious consequences if Italy were prohibited from joining Europe's planned monetary union in 1999.</p>
<p>&quot;There would be a devaluation of the lira,&quot; if Italy were not a member of the currency union from the start, Prodi told journalists after meeting with Germany's Chancellor Helmut Kohl.</p>
<p>&quot;The entire economic policy would have to be reviewed and this is not acceptable,&quot; Prodi added.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
